## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design dynamic topology changes without downtime, while guaranteeing per-key in-order delivery and exactly-once semantics under backpressure. It also probes practical test planning for migration safety and performance.

## Key Concepts
- Runtime topology changes with zero-downtime
- Per-key state migration and sequence tracking
- Bounded buffers and backpressure signaling
- Exactly-once semantics across reconfiguration
- Versioned topology and safe handoff

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch for key handoff
function migrateKey(key, oldWorker, newWorker) {
  // Phase 1: Drain in-flight items
  oldWorker.pauseKey(key);
  await oldWorker.flushKey(key);

  // Phase 2: Transfer state atomically
  const state = oldWorker.getState(key);
  const sequence = oldWorker.getSequence(key);
  newWorker.restoreState(key, state, sequence);

  // Phase 3: Resume processing
  newWorker.resumeKey(key);
}
```

